WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:06.025
First: you change the pre-hire
workflow's offset in its file.

3
00:00:06.025 --> 00:00:07.750
What does the plan produce for it?

4
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.611
The answer is a: a body
for create new version,

5
00:00:10.611 --> 00:00:14.188
because Learn makes a definition
change a new version.

6
00:00:14.188 --> 00:00:15.926
There's no in-place update.

7
00:00:15.926 --> 00:00:19.150
A file with no match in the
tenant would become a create.

8
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:22.200
Second: which hire counts
as ready on day one?

9
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.913
The answer is c: one whose account
exists and is enabled, holds a license,

10
00:00:26.913 --> 00:00:31.625
has the onboarding package delivered,
and has a completed pre-hire run.

11
00:00:31.625 --> 00:00:32.588
All four.

12
00:00:32.588 --> 00:00:35.706
An account that exists but
is disabled isn't ready,

13
00:00:35.706 --> 00:00:38.749
and neither is a pre-hire
run that didn't complete.

14
00:00:38.749 --> 00:00:43.700
The module page has two more questions,
each linked to the section that answers it.
